  "notes": "EWF&#x27;s own 31 July 1997 broadcast opens on a backstage angle in which the operator&#x27;s own self-inserted wrestling persona, Ben &quot;Sexyboy&quot; Toussi, announces his in-ring retirement match for the promotion&#x27;s 10 August pay-per-view and hands the Hardcore Sexyboys stable&#x27;s leadership to Austin Starr. A four-team scramble billed for the EWF United States Tag Team Championship (the Watson Family, SWAT, Higher Danger and Parental Advisory) is called on-air but its own team assignments are too tangled in the surviving text to structure honestly into sides; the broadcast names the Watson Family the new champions and the card&#x27;s own recap is otherwise carried in prose only, not registered as a fifth match."
